# Pairs with Termination. Dropping the weak-fairness conjunct is the sharpest
# possible test of a liveness property: the safety structure of the protocol is
# untouched and every safety invariant still holds, so ONLY a property that
# genuinely depends on the fairness assumption can notice. A Termination check
# that survived this mutation would be checking nothing.
MODULE: TerminationNoFairness
TARGET: Termination
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: drops the weak-fairness conjunct from Spec, so a saga may stall forever

--- FIND
Spec == Init /\ [][Next]_vars /\ \A t \in Txns : WF_vars(TxProgress(t))
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no fairness. Nothing is required to ever take a step, so a saga
\* can stutter in "init" forever.
Spec == Init /\ [][Next]_vars
--- END
